if (terminal != null) return terminal;
```
At this point, `newMessages.last` is `message` (the assistant message just added). `currentContext.messages` — the interceptor doesn't touch the context; the context messages list contains the original message instance. The interceptor replaced the `MessageEndEvent` payload but not the context. So `_emitFinalizeGateFold(newMessages, currentContext.messages, stash, emit)` works there too.

But note: `_emitFinalizeGateFold` is invoked with the wrapped `emit` (the interceptor-wrapped sink). The TaskLedgerEvent is not a MessageEndEvent, so passes through fine.

