No command. With my rule (≥2 entries OR any non-empty command), this doc example → rejected. A genuine near-miss with a single item: `- requirement: X\n  status: pass` with no command → rejected too. Hmm, that's a false negative: a real one-item self-check without command wouldn't be captured. But the gate's value comes from re-verification telemetry; the checklist contract's whole point is the verification command. A ledger without any verification fields is weak anyway. The reviewer's suggestion exactly: "require at least one entry with a real `status`/`command` field, or two-plus entries — so a single `- requirement:` bullet isn't enough to classify a prose section as a ledger."

